# Vault Terminal — 24/7 alert watcher configuration
# Copy to /etc/vault-alerts.env (or export these) and run:
#   node server/alerts-watcher.mjs --once   # test
#   node server/alerts-watcher.mjs          # run forever

# REQUIRED: the secret key of the account whose alerts should be watched.
# Use your own nsec (the one you log into the terminal with) so the watcher
# can also mark alerts as fired on Nostr.
VAULT_NSEC=nsec1...

# OPTIONAL: comma-separated relays to read alerts from and publish to.
# Defaults to a curated public set.
# VAULT_RELAYS=wss://relay.ditto.pub,wss://relay.primal.net,wss://nos.lol

# OPTIONAL: seconds between checks (default 60, minimum 15).
# VAULT_INTERVAL=60

# OPTIONAL: webhook URL that receives a JSON POST whenever an alert fires.
# Point it at ntfy.sh, Pushover, Discord, Slack, etc.
# VAULT_ALERT_WEBHOOK=https://ntfy.sh/your-topic

# OPTIONAL: npub to receive the encrypted Nostr DM (default: the alert owner).
# VAULT_DM_TO=npub1...

# OPTIONAL: set to 1 to disable Nostr DM notifications entirely.
# VAULT_NO_DM=0

# --- Market snapshot pusher (server/market-snapshot.mjs) ---
# Uses VAULT_NSEC + VAULT_RELAYS above. Defaults to snapshotting the owner's
# watchlist (read from Nostr). Override with a comma-separated list:
# VAULT_SNAPSHOT_SYMBOLS=AAPL,NVDA,SPY
# Seconds between runs in --loop mode (default 3600 = hourly):
# VAULT_SNAPSHOT_INTERVAL=3600

# --- SEC fundamentals fetcher (server/sec-fundamentals.mjs) ---
# Uses VAULT_NSEC + VAULT_RELAYS above. Defaults to the US equities in the
# owner's watchlist (Canadian/foreign/crypto/index symbols are skipped — SEC
# covers US filings). Override the symbol list:
# VAULT_SEC_SYMBOLS=AAPL,NVDA,MSFT
# Max symbols per run (SEC-friendly; default 25):
# VAULT_SEC_MAX=25
# Seconds between runs in --loop mode (default 86400 = daily):
# VAULT_SEC_INTERVAL=86400

# --- AI filing analyzer (server/analyzer.mjs, Phase 2) ---
# Model-agnostic — any OpenAI-compatible chat endpoint. DeepSeek:
# ANALYZER_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/v1
# ANALYZER_API_KEY=sk-your-deepseek-key
# ANALYZER_MODEL=deepseek-chat
# …or local Ollama (set a dummy key, model = the pulled one, e.g. llama3.1):
# ANALYZER_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# ANALYZER_API_KEY=ollama
# ANALYZER_MODEL=llama3.1
# Seconds between request-watch cycles in loop mode (default 60):
# ANALYZER_INTERVAL=60
